[Event "QGD: Orthodox 4.Bg5"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 {Take your share of the center.} 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit.} e6 {Decline: protect d5 with a pawn.} 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 {Unpin your knight.} 5. e3 O-O {Castle early.} 6. Nf3 h6 7. Bh4 b6 {Your light bishop goes to b7.} 8. Bd3 Bb7 9. O-O Nbd7 {Everything developed. Solid game.} *

[Event "QGD: Exchange Variation"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 exd5 {Take back with the pawn – your bishop on c8 can breathe.} 5. Bg5 c6 {Make d5 rock solid.} 6. e3 Be7 7. Bd3 Nbd7 8. Qc2 O-O 9. Nf3 Re8 {Rook to the open file.} 10. O-O Nf8 {The knight protects your king.} *

[Event "QGD: 3.Nf3 and 5.Bf4"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 Be7 5. Bf4 O-O 6. e3 c5 {Hit the center from the side.} 7. dxc5 Bxc5 8. a3 Nc6 9. Qc2 Qa5 {Pin the knight and get active.} *

[Event "Trap (Black): The Elephant Trap"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nbd7 {Looks like it leaves d5 weak – but it is a trap!} 5. cxd5 exd5 6. Nxd5 {White grabs a pawn. A mistake!} Nxd5 {Take the knight.} 7. Bxd8 {White takes your queen…} Bb4+ {…but now you give check!} 8. Qd2 Bxd2+ 9. Kxd2 Kxd8 {You win a whole piece.} *

[Event "London System (Black)"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 {The London System.} Nf6 3. e3 c5 {Hit d4 right away.} 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nd2 e6 6. Ngf3 Bd6 {Trade off White's best bishop.} 7. Bg3 O-O 8. Bd3 b6 {Your other bishop goes to b7.} *

[Event "1.d4 d5 2.Nf3 (Black)"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. e3 e6 4. Bd3 c5 {Fight for the center.} 5. b3 Nc6 6. O-O Bd6 7. Bb2 O-O {Castle. Both sides are solid.} *
